<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Lonrho Sugar lifts yr share, div.</title>
<headline>Lonrho Sugar lifts yr share, div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31, 1997</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)		 99.7	  vs 83.8</p>
<p>    Div (cts) 25.0 making 45.0	  vs 40.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	  119.19	 vs 99.63</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		  289.30	 vs 202.25</p>
<p>    Tax			 63.95	 vs 33.53</p>
<p>    Turnover	     1,053.80	 vs 723.78</p>
<p>Div payable June 27 on register June 6</p>
<p>Full name: Lonrho Sugar Corporation Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said it posted record profits in the year under review and sugar production was 512,000 tonnes from the previous year's 467,000.</p>
<p>- The group said it expected to benefit from the acquisitions and restructuring put in place during the past year.</p>
<p>- The company said its results were posted in Swaziland's currency the Emalangeni which is on par with the South African rand.</p>
<p>- Illovo Sugar Ltd said on Thursday it had bought Lonrho Sugar Corp from U.K-based Lonrho Plc for over 1.6 billion rand.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
